From 625b29fc4fd843f7ff0e0f3704137ac3208d0e38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leon Silcott <leon@boasi.io>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:50:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2159/2165] media: imx681: write exposure through the 24-bit
 latch

Use the coarse-integration latch initialized by the sensor mode table.
The inherited 16-bit 0x0202 write did not change brightness in the
upstream author's fixed-light experiment.

Adapted from Leon Silcott's correction in ooaklee/linux_ms_dev_kit-sp11,
linked below. No frame-timing or sensor-table changes are included.
Local fixed-gain RAW tests on a Surface Pro 11 confirmed monotonic
brightness response and return to the initial level, including a stream
restart. Automatic-exposure tuning and suspend/resume are not qualified.

Link: https://github.com/ooaklee/linux_ms_dev_kit-sp11/commit/b1754869f458
(cherry picked from commit 2318c43168f7a7c4238aecb7c1ebf24d88ab7f9c)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/imx681.c b/drivers/media/i2c/imx681.c
index cf99dd211dc0e1d5ccec6ad9edea095d53bc32af..b963373951de74ad36414bacc995dba3271ff65e 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx681.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx681.c
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@
 #define IMX681_MODE_STREAMING	1
 #define IMX681_MODE_STANDBY	0
 #define IMX681_REG_GROUP_HOLD	CCI_REG8(0x0104)
-#define IMX681_REG_EXPOSURE	CCI_REG16(0x0202)
+#define IMX681_REG_EXPOSURE	CCI_REG24(0x0229)
 #define IMX681_REG_ANALOG_GAIN	CCI_REG16(0x0204)
 #define IMX681_REG_DIGITAL_GAIN	CCI_REG16(0x020e)
 #define IMX681_REG_FRAME_LENGTH	CCI_REG16(0x0340)
